From 49546f512dd956b5849f5a164772f5ab3fb91c63 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: benrichard-amd <ben.richard@amd.com>
Date: Tue, 28 Jul 2026 14:10:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] rocprofiler-systems: add ppc64le support

RT library (rocprof-sys-rt):
- Add RTthread-powerpc.c, RTthread-powerpc-asm.S, and
  RTstatic_ctors_dtors-ppc64.c copied from the Dyninst submodule
  (external/dyninst, commit 5dff47b) for ppc64le thread locking
  and static constructor/destructor support.
- Make CMakeLists.txt arch-conditional: select x86 or ppc64 sources
  based on CMAKE_SYSTEM_PROCESSOR.

DL library (rocprof-sys-dl) __libc_start_main interposition:
- On ppc64le ELFv2, _start passes a startup_info struct pointer in r8
  and the stack pointer in r9, rather than individual arguments in
  r3-r7 as on x86_64. The startup_info struct resides in read-only
  memory.
- Add an assembly trampoline (main_ppc64le.S) that saves/restores all
  registers around a C patching function, and tail-calls the real
  __libc_start_main.
- The C patching function copies the read-only startup_info to a
  writable static, swaps the main pointer to rocprofsys_main, and
  returns the copy. Uses dlvsym with glibc version tags to resolve
  the real __libc_start_main without recursion.

Runtime feature guards (config.cpp):
- Disable USE_SAMPLING, USE_PROCESS_SAMPLING, and TRACE (perfetto) on
  ppc64le with warning messages. Signal-based call-stack sampling
  crashes due to a known libunwind ppc64 mixed-frame unwinding
  limitation, and perfetto tracing hits a null dereference on ppc64le.
  Wall-clock profiling (-P) remains fully functional.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
